AOWIS DVMDB — Debian installation
=================================

Binary:        /usr/bin/aowis-server-dvmdb
Service:       aowis-server-dvmdb.service
Vendor unit:   /usr/lib/systemd/system/aowis-server-dvmdb.service
Configuration: /etc/aowis/aowis-server-dvmdb.ini
Storage root:  /var/lib/aowis-dvmdb
Listener:      127.0.0.1:8755 (default)

The package creates an unprivileged aowis-dvmdb system account. systemd
StateDirectory=aowis-dvmdb provisions the persistent storage root with
mode 0700. The package never removes that data directory during remove or
purge. The INI is a dpkg-managed conffile: local edits are preserved on
upgrade/removal and the file is removed by purge.

The packaged vendor unit runs /usr/bin/aowis-server-dvmdb, not the
/usr/local/bin path used by the manual-install deploy/ example.

Administration:

  sudo systemctl status aowis-server-dvmdb
  sudo journalctl -u aowis-server-dvmdb -f
  sudo systemctl edit aowis-server-dvmdb

Ready check:

  curl -fsS http://127.0.0.1:8755/dvmdb/v1/ready

SECURITY: DVMDB currently has no HTTP authentication or authorization and
does not serve HTTPS directly. Keep its listener loopback-only unless it
is reachable exclusively over a trusted network and protected separately.
TLS by itself does not provide user authorization.
